+*------------------------------------------------------------------*
+|CS              DLC             LDLC           DMUX            UDP|
+*------------------------------------------------------------------*
+ .                .               .              .               .
+ .             DEACT              .      DISC    .      DISC     . DISC
+ o<-------------------------------o<-------------o<--------------o<-----
+ |                .               |             DM               . DM
+ |                .               *----------------------------->o----->
+ | DISCONNECT(RQ) .    destroy    .              .               .
+ *--------------->o-------------->o              .               .
+ .DISCONNECT(RSP) |                              .               .
+ o<---------------*                              .               .
+]]></artwork>
+          <t indent="0" pn="section-2.5.1-23">Figure 6. Regular TG Deactivation (incoming)</t>
+          <t indent="0" pn="section-2.5.1-24">In Figure 6, when an adjacent node deactivates a TG, the local node
+receives a DISC.  CS sends STOP_LS(IND) to NOF.  Because IP is
+connectionless, the DLC manager is not aware that the link has been
+deactivated.  For that reason, CS also needs to send DISCONNECT(RQ)
+to the DLC manager; the DLC manager deactivates the instance of LDLC.</t>
